    # We tile the (i,j,k) space into blocks (TI,TJ,TK). For each (I,J)
    # tile of tmp, we:
    #   - zero the tmp tile;
    #   - sweep k in TK-sized tiles, accumulating partial products.
    #
    # For a fixed (i,j), the sequence of operations is:
    #   tmp[i,j] = 0
    #   then for k = 0..nk-1 in order:
    #       tmp[i,j] += alpha*A[i,k]*B[k,j]
    # which is exactly the same as the original kernel (only the work
    # for different (i,j) pairs is interleaved).
